a and Asia-Pacific Studies from broader theoretical perspectives, to engage in academic discourse and policy debate about implications of China rising, to reflect on their four-year learning experience in Ithaca, Washington, D.C., and Beijing as students of contemporary China studies, and to enhance their abilities to pursue future studies and/or careers that are related to their CAPS\u00a0experience after graduating from Cornell.\u00a0 The seminar is organized around the central theme - China rising - and roughly divided into three sections:\u00a0 (1) China's rise and the \"paradigm change\" in world politics; (2) China's quest for identity and order; and (3) implications of China rising for the U.S. and the world.\u00a0 Under each of these sections, a few specific topics are identified for class discussion.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-UGR)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2692, "crseId": 364033, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "CAPS", "catalogNbr": "4888", "titleShort": "Directed Study - Beijing", "titleLong": "Directed Study - Beijing", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "671", "classNbr": 18984, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "03:00PM", "timeEnd": "06:00PM", "startDt": "03/01/2018", "endDt": "06/01/2018", "instructors": [], "pattern": "R", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": null}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descr